  {
   "group": "01M5AX9V1JKRPK91EJ08ZJ5CJV",
   "author": "FooBarrington@lemmy.world",
   "user": "FooBarrington@lemmy.world",
   "date": "2026-11-07T20:40:57Z",
   "title": "[Discussion] How do you (unit-)test your shaders?",
   "text": "Hey all! I’ve been thinking about how to best unit-test my shader code, since TDD has been very helpful for me. But I’ve been able to find surprisingly little information. If possible, I’d love to hear from your experiences!"
  },
  {
   "group": "01M6H1DWNEPEGAP2GM9QDVS135",
   "author": "Nelfaneor",
   "user": "nelfan@gotosocial.social",
   "date": "2026-11-07T20:03:51Z",
   "title": "",
   "text": "Your social media strategy is important too and I’m very pleased and relieved to find you and your party on the #Fediverse. The ideal and best tool to manage your proposition is @Bonfire_Networks in order to organise a long-term interactive discussion about it."
  },
  {
   "group": "01M5AX9V1JKRPK91EJ08ZJ5CJV",
   "author": "MousePotatoDoesStuff",
   "user": "MousePotatoDoesStuff@piefed.social",
   "date": "2026-11-07T19:48:54Z",
   "title": "How to expand a Control object to fill its H/Vbox container in Godot 4",
   "text": "Been struggling with this for too long before discovering this, made this video so you don’t have to. Tested with Godot 4.8, but this feature has probably been around since 4.0."
  },
  {
   "group": "01M4CFA3PH5ESAX6HKBZV5RZPA",
   "author": "bretton.dev",
   "user": "bretton.dev@coves.social",
   "date": "2026-11-07T00:40:11Z",
   "title": "How private do you consider your votes in the Threadiverse?",
   "text": "From the technical side anyone can spin up their own Lemmy instance and view all votes, but I’m curious at what the community’s perspective on how “private” that is. I think Mbin already shows upvoters? Piefed allows anonymous voting."
  },
  {
   "group": "01M6H1DWNEPEGAP2GM9QDVS135",
   "author": "Misha Velthuis",
   "user": "misha@bonfire.opentech-auc.org",
   "date": "2026-11-06T11:24:26Z",
   "title": "Organize groups?",
   "text": "Would it be an idea to allow people to organize groups in categories or spaces? So let’s say on our Bonfire instance there would be a space called “Courses”, which would then contain all the groups of AUC courses?"
  },
  {
